---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Tips | Where Horses Run"
  description="How optional tips for information and content already provided by Where Horses Run work."
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">Payments</p>
    <h1 id="page-title">Optional tips</h1>
    <p class="hero__summary">Where Horses Run publishes its information free of charge. A tip, if enabled, is a discretionary payment in appreciation for information and content already provided before payment.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section-grid" aria-label="Tip policy">
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Content is provided before payment</h2>
      <p>Calendar, racecourse, country, glossary, and official-source information is available without a tip. A tip does not unlock paid membership, a subscription, exclusive content, or future access.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Not donations or fundraising</h2>
      <p>Tips are not donations, fundraising, crowdfunding, preorders, or contributions to a funding campaign. There is no funding goal, charitable purpose, campaign reward, or promise of future development in exchange for payment.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>What a tip means</h2>
      <p>A tip is an optional payment in appreciation for information and content already provided by Where Horses Run. It does not purchase a betting service, prediction, racecard, odds, prize, or preferential access.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>No third-party collection</h2>
      <p>Where Horses Run accepts payments only for its own content. It does not collect money on behalf of other people, charities, campaigns, organizations, or third-party content creators.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>No wagering</h2>
      <p>Where Horses Run does not accept bets, transmit wagers, provide gambling accounts, or pay gambling winnings. Tips are unrelated to the outcome of any race.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Payment availability</h2>
      <p>Tip payments are not yet enabled. If enabled, the amount, currency, payment processor, and applicable policies will be shown before payment.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Payment questions</h2>
      <p>See the <a href="/refund/">Refund Policy</a>, <a href="/commercial-disclosure/">Commerce Disclosure</a>, and <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> pages.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
